From: Pavel Bragin <pabragin@yandex.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: allow disabling the NPU offload

Traffic that the host itself sends or receives over Wi-Fi (VPN, local
services) is copied by the AN7552 NPU and tops out at ~150 Mbit/s on
the Xiaomi BE5000, while the plain mt76 path reaches ~900 Mbit/s. Add
npu_enable (default on) so that such setups can skip the NPU.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Bragin <pabragin@yandex.ru>
---
diff --git a/mt7996/pci.c b/mt7996/pci.c
index 3d0a0e2..f647f8e 100644
--- a/mt7996/pci.c
+++ b/mt7996/pci.c
@@ -11,6 +11,10 @@
 #include "mac.h"
 #include "../trace.h"
 
+static bool npu_enable = true;
+module_param(npu_enable, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(npu_enable, "Use the NPU for Wi-Fi offload");
+
 static LIST_HEAD(hif_list);
 static DEFINE_SPINLOCK(hif_lock);
 static u32 hif_idx;
@@ -152,8 +156,9 @@ static int mt7996_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 	if (hif2)
 		pci_set_master(to_pci_dev(hif2->dev));
 
-	ret = mt76_npu_init(mdev, pci_resource_start(pdev, 0),
-			    pci_domain_nr(pdev->bus) ? 3 : 2);
+	ret = npu_enable ? mt76_npu_init(mdev, pci_resource_start(pdev, 0),
+					 pci_domain_nr(pdev->bus) ? 3 : 2) :
+			   -ENODEV;
 	if (ret && ret != -ENODEV && ret != -EOPNOTSUPP)
 		goto free_device;
 
